  "description": "Under the fixture policy a directive does not end the change story at the review: the baseline end act is recorded and reported as the baseline ending, while the story stays open under its policy, reviewed and therefore not pending, with the directive's expectation as its open child. A-601's lacquer fulfils the expectation; that write records the policy end act, cause directive_closed, citing the fulfilling Assertion at the qualifying moment, beside the property's own end act. The story's interval stays the baseline interval.",
  "note": "7.6.7: \"An expectation property whose first period is nested under exactly one story (7.6.15), because a review of that story began it, is part of that story, its middle: its begin and end acts, and the revisions of them (7.6.10), are Assertions on that story Item in the same form, `(story, <event context>, story)`.\" The act names follow README section 7, Story-held expectation property acts: `(<story>, \"<story>/exp:<path>/b<n>\", <story>)`, with `/e<n>` and `/v<n>` likewise.",
